ol_014 + mol_002.\",\n        \"Annotate rxn_002 with 254 nm UV, phosphate, pH about 7, and CuCN as catalyst metadata.\",\n        \"If compactness allows, add acetaldehyde over-reduction and Ser-CN loss channels as optional sinks.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P2\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.95,\n        \"rxn_002\": 0.9,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.97,\n        \"rxn_007\": 0.71\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.86,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.94,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.76,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.87,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.83,\n      \"feedback\": \"Upstream chemistry is strong, but the final hydrolysis step is weaker environmentally. rxn_007 also needs 2 H2O, and the title geothermal-cycling conflicts with the Biochemical environment label. If genuinely hot conditions are intended, serine degradation becomes a significant competing sink.\",\n      \"approved\": true,\n      \"problematic_reactions\": [\n        \"rxn_007\"\n      ],\n      \"suggestions\": [\n        \"Write rxn_007 explicitly as mol_011 + 2 mol_003 -> mol_014 + mol_002.\",\n        \"Replace Biochemical with a physical prebiotic setting such as mild geothermal wet-dry cycling and specify temperature bounds.\",\n        \"Explain transfer or concentration of Ser-CN from the surface photoredox setting to the hydrolysis setting.\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n      \"reaction_scores\": {\n        \"rxn_001\": 0.95,\n        \"rxn_003\": 0.84,\n        \"rxn_005\": 0.97,\n        \"rxn_006\": 0.78\n      },\n      \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.87,\n      \"pathway_coherence\": 0.94,\n      \"environmental_progression\": 0.9,\n      \"target_achievement\": 0.91,\n      \"overall_confidence\": 0.87,\n      \"feedback\": \"Good all-surface variant with literature support for copper-free H2S photoreduction, though the reduction step is less efficient than the CuCN-assisted case. rxn_